          "traits": [
            "Melee Weapon§Dragon Knights—Drakesteed Fangs and Talons",
            "Ranged Weapon§Dragon Knights—Laser Lance",
            "Ranged Weapon§Dragon Knights—Solar Carbine",
            "Melee Weapon§Dragon Knights—Laser Lance"
          ]
        }
      },
      "Battle Trait§The Falling Blade": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Howling Banshees",
            "Shining Spears",
            "Striking Scorpions"
          ]
        },
        "text": "You can re-roll Charge rolls made for this unit."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Soulseeing": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Psyker"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Ranged weapons equipped by models in this unit (excluding **^^Support Weapon^^** models) have the **[IGNORES COVER]** ability, and each time a model in this unit (excluding **^^Support Weapon^^** models) makes a ranged attack, you can ignore any or all modifiers to that attack's Ballistic Skill characteristic and/or any or all modifiers to the Hit roll."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Psy-prism": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Psyker"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Psychic weapons equipped by models in this unit have the **[SUSTAINED HITS 2]** ability."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Fallen Foreseen": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Psyker"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time a model in this unit is destroyed by a ranged attack, roll one D6: on a 3+, do not remove it from play. The destroyed model can shoot after the attacking unit has finished making its attacks, and is then removed from play."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Crystalline Targeting Matrix": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Vehicle"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Ranged weapons equipped by models in this unit have the **[ASSAULT]** ability."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Hallucinogen Launchers": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Vehicle"
          ]
        },
        "text": "This unit has the **^^Smoke^^** keyword, and you can target it with the Smokescreen Stratagem for 0CP."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Star Engines": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Vehicle"
          ]
        },
        "text": "This unit is eligible to shoot in a turn in which it Fell Back."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Desperate Protectors": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Guardians"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time you target this unit with the Fire Overwatch Stratagem, hits are scored on unmodified Hit rolls of 5+ while resolving that Stratagem. If this unit, is within range of one or more objective markers, hits are scored on unmodified Hit rolls of 4+ instead."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Sombre Determination": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Guardians"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Add 1 to the Objective Control characteristic of models in this unit."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Seasoned Protectors": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Guardians"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Ranged weapons equipped by models in this unit have the **[HEAVY]** ability."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Fell the Mighty": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Asuryani"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time a melee attack made by a model in this unit is allocated to a **^^Monster^^** or **^^Vehicle^^** model, add 1 to the Damage characteristic of that attack."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Graceful Advance": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Asuryani"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Models in this unit have the Scouts 8\" ability."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Preternatural Acrobatics": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Asuryani"
          ]
        },
        "text": "This unit is eligible to declare a charge in a turn in which it Advanced."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Farstrike": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Dark Reapers",
            "Dire Avengers",
            "Fire Dragons",
            "Swooping Hawks",
            "Warp Spiders"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Add 6\" to the Range characteristic of ranged weapons equipped by models in this unit. For each of those weapons with the **[TORRENT]**, add 3\" to the Range characteristic of that weapon instead."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Way of Stone": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Dark Reapers",
            "Dire Avengers",
            "Fire Dragons",
            "Swooping Hawks",
            "Warp Spiders"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time a ranged attack targets this unit, if the Strength characteristic of that attack is greater than this unit's Toughness characteristic, subtract 1 from the Wound roll."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Hunter's Eye": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Dark Reapers",
            "Dire Avengers",
            "Fire Dragons",
            "Swooping Hawks",
            "Warp Spiders"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time a model in this unit makes a ranged attack that targets an enemy unit within half range, improve the Armour Penetration characteristic of that attack by 1."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Bladeweave": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Howling Banshees",
            "Shining Spears",
            "Striking Scorpions"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time a melee attack targets this unit, subtract 1 from the Wound roll."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Shadowswift": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Howling Banshees",
            "Shining Spears",
            "Striking Scorpions"
          ]
        },
        "text": "This unit cannot be targeted by ranged attacks unless the attacking model is within 18\"."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Spitefire": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Kabal"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Assault weapons equipped by models in this unit have the **[RAPID FIRE 1]** ability. All other ranged weapons equipped by models in this unit have the **[ASSAULT]** ability."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Kabalite Trueborn": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Kabalite Warriors",
            "Hand of the Archon"
          ]
        },
        "text": "**^^Kabalite Warriors^^** or **^^Hand of the Archon^^** unit only. Improve the Leadership characteristic of models in this unit by 1 and improve the Ballistic Skill characteristic of ranged weapons equipped by models in this unit by 1."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Hekatrix Bloodbrides": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Wyches"
          ]
        },
        "text": "**^^Wychs^^** unit only. Improve the Leadership characteristic of models in this unit by 1 and improve the Weapon Skill characteristic of melee weapons equipped by models in this unit by 1."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Haemoxytes": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Wracks"
          ]
        },
        "text": "**^^Wracks^^** unit only. Improve the Leadership and Save characteristics of models in this unit by 1."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Living Atrocities (Aura)": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Haemonculus Covens"
          ]
        },
        "text": "While an enemy unit is within 6\" of this unit, each time that enemy unit fails a Battle-shock test, it suffers D3 mortal wounds (a unit cannot suffer more than 3 mortal wounds per turn as a result of this Battle Trait)."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Baleful Armaments (Pain)": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Haemonculus Covens"
          ]
        },
        "text": "In your Shooting phase, when you select this unit to shoot, you can spend 1 Pain token to Empower this unit. While Empowered, ranged weapons equipped by models in this unit have the **[HAZARDOUS]** ability and each time an attack is made with such a weapon, add 1 to the Damage characteristic of that attack."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Scabhide": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Haemonculus Covens"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time an attack with an unmodified Damage characteristic of 1 is allocated to a model in this unit, add 1 to any armour saving throw made against that attack."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Slashing Impact": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Wych Cult"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time this unit ends a Charge move, select one enemy unit within Engagement Range of it, then roll one D6 for each model in this unit that is within Engagement Range of that enemy unit: for each 4+, that enemy unit suffers 1 mortal wound (to a maximum of 6 mortal wounds)."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Inescapable (Pain)": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Kabal"
          ]
        },
        "text": "In your Shooting phase, when you select this unit to shoot, you can spend 1 Pain token to Empower this unit. While Empowered, ranged weapons equipped by models in this unit have the **[IGNORES COVER]** ability."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Claws of the Archon": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Kabal"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Add 1 to the Objective Control characteristic of models in this unit."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Scent of the Kill": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Wych Cult"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time a model in this unit makes a Pile-in or Consolidation move, it can move up to 6\" instead of up to 3\"."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Knife Dancers (Pain)": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Wych Cult"
          ]
        },
        "text": "In the Fight phase, when you select this unit to fight, you can spend 1 Pain token to Empower this unit. While Empowered, each time a model in this unit makes a melee attack that targets an **^^Infantry^^** unit, that attack has the **[LETHAL HITS]** ability."
      },
      "Crusade Relic§Shimmerplume of Achillrial": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Antiquity Relic"
          ]
        },
        "text": "**^^Autarch^^** model only. Each time a ranged attack targets the bearer's unit, subtract 1 from the Hit roll and subtract 1 from the Wound roll.",
        "stats": {
          "Crusade Pts": {
            "value": 2
          }
        },
        "rules": {
          "Autarch only.": {
            "evals": [
              {
                "actionable": true,
                "contains": true,
                "not": false,
                "operator": "AND",
                "paths": [
                  [
                    "{parent}",
                    "keywords",
                    "Keywords"
                  ]
                ],
                "value": "Autarch"
              }
            ],
            "evaluate": "AND",
            "failState": "error"
          }
        }
      },
      "Crusade Relic§Kaela Mensha Shelwe, Song of the Bloody-handed": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Legendary Relic"
          ]
        },
        "text": "**^^Asuryani^^** model only. The bearer's melee weapons have the **[ANTI-BEASTS 3+]]**, **[ANTI-INFANTRY 3+]]**, **[ANTI-MOUNTED 3+]]** and **[DEVASTATING WOUNDS]]** abilities. In addition, at the end of the Fight phase, if the bearer destroyed one or more enemy models that phase (excluding **^^Vehicles^^**), the bearer regains up to D3 lost wounds.",
        "stats": {
          "Crusade Pts": {
            "value": 3
          }
        }
      },
      "Crusade Relic§Rune of Faolchú": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Artificer Relic"
          ]
        },
        "text": "**^^Aeldari^^** model only. At the end of your Movement phase, select one enemy unit within 18\" of and visible to the bearer. Until the end of your next Movement phase, each time a friendly **^^Aeldari^^** model makes an attack that targets that unit, improve the Armour Penetration characteristic of that attack by 1.",
        "rules": {
          "Aeldari only.": {
            "evals": [
              {
                "actionable": true,
                "contains": true,
                "not": false,
                "operator": "AND",
                "paths": [
                  [
                    "{parent}",
                    "keywords",
                    "Keywords"
                  ]
                ],
                "value": "Aeldari"
              }
            ],
            "evaluate": "AND",
            "failState": "error"
          }
        }
      },
      "Crusade Relic§Banner of Asuryan": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Artificer Relic"
          ]
        },
        "text": "**^^Autarch^^** model only. At the start of the battle round, if the bearer is on the battlefield, you gain 1 additional Battle Focus token.",
        "rules": {
          "Autarch only.": {
            "evals": [
              {
                "actionable": true,
                "contains": true,
                "not": false,
                "operator": "AND",
                "paths": [
                  [
                    "{parent}",
                    "keywords",
                    "Keywords"
                  ]
                ],
                "value": "Autarch"
              }
            ],
            "evaluate": "AND",
            "failState": "error"
          }
        }
      },
      "Requisition§Consult the Runes": {
        "stats": {
          "RP": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "Purchase this Requisition when your Crusade force begins Guiding Fate, just after you generate your Crusade force’s Threads of Fate. Select one of those Threads of Fate and replace it with a randomly selected Thread of Fate that was not selected for your Crusade force. You can only purchase this Requisition once for each time your Crusade force is Guiding Fate."
      },
      "Requisition§Burned Futures": {
        "stats": {
          "RP": {
            "value": 2
          }
        },
        "text": "Purchase this Requisition just after a battle, if your Crusade force is Guiding Fate. Your Crusade forces Threat does not increase for this battle, and if any of your Crusade forces Threads of Fate would move to their next stage or end in failure this battle, they do not move to the next stage and do not end in failure, remaining at their current stages instead. You can only purchase this Requisition once for each time your Crusade force is Guiding Fate."
      },
      "Requisition§Spiritual Necromancy": {
        "stats": {
          "RP": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "Purchase this Requisition when an ASURYANI INFANTRY unit from your Crusade force (excluding WRAITH CONSTRUCT units) would gain a second or subsequent Battle Scar. Remove that unit from your Order of Battle and replace it with one WRAITH CONSTRUCT unit. You cannot purchase this Requisition if doing so would cause your total Crusade points to exceed your Crusade forces Supply Limit. The new unit starts with the same number of XP as the unit it replaced and gains the appropriate number of Battle Honours for its rank. You can re-roll Out Of Action tests taken for the new unit."
      },
      "Requisition§Paths of the Aeldari": {
        "stats": {
          "RP": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "Purchase this Requisition after a battle. Select one ASURYANI INFANTRY unit (excluding CHARACTER and WRAITH CONSTRUCT units) on your Order of Battle. Remove that unit from your Order of Battle and replace it with another, different ASURYANI INFANTRY unit (excluding CHARACTER and WRAITH CONSTRUCT units). You cannot purchase this Requisition if doing so would cause your total Crusade points to exceed your Crusade forces Supply Limit. The new unit starts with the same number of XP as the unit it replaced, gains the appropriate number of Battle Honours for its rank and retains the PATH OF THE WARRIOR keyword if it had it. It then gains an additional D3+1XP and, if the new unit has the ASPECT WARRIORS keyword, it gains the PATH OF THE WARRIOR keyword if it does not have it already."
      },
      "Requisition§Court of the Young King": {
        "stats": {
          "RP": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "Purchase this Requisition before a battle, if you do not have an AVATAR OF KHAINE model on your Order of Battle and your Crusade force is Guiding Fate. Select one ASPECT WARRIORS unit on your Order of Battle; that ASPECT WARRIORS unit gains a Battle Scar and you can add one AVATAR OF KHAINE model to your Order of Battle. The points value of that Avatar of Khaine model does not count towards your Crusade force’s Supply Used. Once your Crusade force is no longer Guiding Fate, you must remove that AVATAR OF KHAINE model from your Order of Battle."
      },
      "Requisition§Manifest the Yncarne": {
        "stats": {
          "RP": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "Purchase this Requisition after a battle that you lost, if you have a YVRAINE model on your Order of Battle but do not have a THE YNCARNE model on it, and if your Crusade force is Guiding Fate. You can add one THE YNCARNE model to your Order of Battle. The points value of that THE YNCARNE model does not count towards your Crusade forces Supply Used. Once your Crusade force is no longer Guiding Fate, you must remove that THE YNCARNE model from your Order of Battle."
      },
      "Crusade Badge§Seer of the Fates": {
        "text": "You have perceived that which threatens your craftworld in the days to come. Through bloodshed and cunning you have turned aside that peril and - though no war comes without cost - you have done much to defend your people and their home.\nYou have won at least two battles.\nYour Crusade force has completed at least one Guiding Fate with a final Threat of 12 or lower."
      },
      "Crusade Badge§Seeker of the Ways": {
        "text": "Your Crusade force has completed at least two Guiding Fates.\nYou have won at least six battles.\nYour Crusade force has completed at least one Guiding Fate with a final Threat of 8 or lower."
      },
      "Crusade Badge§Saviour of the Future": {
        "text": "Your Crusade force has completed at least three Guiding Fates.\nYou have won at least ten battles.\nYour Crusade force has completed at least one Guiding Fate with a final Threat of 4 or lower."
      },
      "Aeldari Path Trait§Footfalls of Fate": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Path of the Seer"
          ]
        },
        "text": "You can re-roll Advance rolls made for this unit and, in your Movement phase, each time a model in it moves, it can move through enemy models (excluding **^^Monsters^^** and **^^Vehicles^^**). When doing so, it can move within Engagement Range of such models but cannot end that move within Engagement Range of them and any Desperate Escape test is automatically passed."
      },
      "Aeldari Path Trait§Webway Spar": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Path of the Seer"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Once per turn, at the end of your Movement phase, one unit from your Crusade army with this ability can use it. If it does, roll one D6: on a 1, that unit suffers D3 mortal wounds; on a 2+, remove that unit from the battlefield and set it up again anywhere on the battlefield that is more than 9\" horizontally away from all enemy units. Each unit can only use this ability once per battle."
      },
      "Aeldari Path Trait§Spirit of Eldanesh": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Path of the Seer"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Psychic weapons equipped by models in this unit unit have the **[ANTI-MONSTER 3+]** and **[ANTI-VEHICLE 3+]** abilities."
      },
      "Aeldari Path Trait§Paths of the Pathless": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Path of Command"
          ]
        },
        "text": "At the start of the first battle round, before any moves are made using the Scouts ability, one unit from your Crusade army with this ability can use it. If it does, you can select up to two friendly **^^Aeldari Infantry^^** units within 6\" of that unit that do not have the Scouts ability. Until the end of the battle, all models in the selected units have the Scouts 6\" ability."
      },
      "Aeldari Path Trait§Strategic Philosopher": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Path of Command"
          ]
        },
        "text": "In your Command phase, if this unit is within range of one or more objective markers you control and it is not Battle-shocked, roll one D6: on a 3+, you gain 1CP."
      },
      "Aeldari Path Trait§Master Misdirector": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Path of Command"
          ]
        },
        "text": "After both players have deployed their armies, one unit from your Crusade army with this ability can use it. If it does, select up to two **^^Aeldari^^** units from your Crusade army and redeploy them. When doing so, you can set those units up in Strategic Reserves if you wish, regardless of how many units are already in Strategic Reserves."
      },
      "Aeldari Path Trait§Dead-eye Shots": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Path of the Warrior"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Ranged weapons equipped by models in this unit have the **[PRECISION]** ability."
      },
      "Aeldari Path Trait§Khaine's Vengeance": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Path of the Warrior"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time an enemy unit within Engagement Range of this unit is selected to Fall Back, roll one D6, subtracting 2 if that unit is a **^^Monster^^** or **^^Vehicle^^**: on a 2+, that unit suffers D3 mortal wounds."
      },
      "Aeldari Path Trait§Tactical Teachings": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Path of the Warrior"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time a ranged attack targets this unit, if this unit is within range or one or more objective markers, models in this unit have the Benefit of Cover against this attack."
      },
      "Aeldari Path Trait§Nimble Fighters": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Path of the Warrior"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time a melee attack targets this unit, subtract 1 from the Hit roll."
      },
      "Aeldari Path Trait§Battlewraiths": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Path of the Warrior"
          ]
        },
        "text": "In your Shooting phase, after this unit has shot, it can make a Normal move of up to D6\". If it does, until the end of the turn, this unit is not eligible to declare a charge."
      },
      "Aeldari Path Trait§Sunshock Fire Patterns": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Path of the Warrior"
          ]
        },
        "text": "In your Shooting phase, after this unit has shot, select one enemy unit hit by one or more of those attacks. That enemy unit must take a Battle-shock test."
      },
      "Ability§Thread of Fate: Destined Device": {
        "text": "**Buried Provenance (Dawning):** If the device is never discovered, its perilous potential will never be realised.\n\nAt the start of the Deploy Crusade Armies step, select one objective marker on the battlefield. In your opponent’s Command phase, if they control that objective marker, they can select one unit within range of it. That unit gains 3XP and that objective marker is removed from the battlefield.\n\nAt the end of the battle, if that objective marker is on the battlefield and you control it, your Crusade army finds the device and this Thread of Fate ends successfully.\n\n**Unknowing Bearer (Waning):** At the start of the first battle round, your opponent must select three units from their army that are on the battlefield or embarked within a TRANSPORT that is on the battlefield. Randomly determine one of those units to be carrying the device.\n\nAt the end of the battle, if the unit that was carrying the device is destroyed, this Thread of Fate ends successfully.\n\n**Abandoned (Frayed):** Having tricked the bearer of the device, the Aeldari have a last chance to snatch it away.\n\nAt the start of the Deploy Crusade Armies step, randomly select one objective marker on the battlefield. If the mission does not have any objective markers, set one up in the centre of the battlefield.\n\nIn your Command phase, if you control that objective marker, roll one D6: on a 5+, you have found the device and this Thread of Fate ends successfully."
      },
      "Ability§Thread of Fate: Rising Nemesis": {
        "text": "**Sow Dissent (Dawning):** At the start of the first battle round, your opponent’s army has a Dissension tally of 0. Each lime an enemy unit fails a Battle-shock test, add 1 to your opponent’s army’s Dissension tally.\n\nAt the end of the battle, if your opponent’s army’s Dissension tally is at least twice the number of CHARACTER models on your opponent’s Army Roster, this Thread of Fate ends successfully.\n\n**Sever the Head (Waning):** At the start of the first battle round, select three models from your opponent’s army. These must be CHARACTER models, if possible, and one of them must be your opponent’s WARLORD.\n\nAt the end of the battle, if all three of the selected models are destroyed, this Thread of Fate ends successfully.\n\n**Seal the Webway (Frayed):** At the start of the Deploy Crusade Armies step, select two objective markers on the battlefield wholly within No Man’s Land. In your Shooting phase, for each of the selected objective markers, you can select one AELDARI PSYKER model from your Crusade army within 9\" of that objective marker and not within Engagement Range of one or more enemy units. If you do, that objective marker gains 1 Sealing point. At the end of the battle, if both selected objective markers have 2 or more Sealing points, this Thread of Fate ends successfully."
      },
      "Ability§Thread of Fate: Humble Beginnings": {
        "text": "**Destined for Greatness (Dawning):** At the start of the first battle round, select one AELDARI INFANTRY unit from your Crusade army (excluding Attached units) that is on the battlefield or embarked within a TRANSPORT that is on the battlefield. This must be a GUARDIANS unit if possible.\n\nIf a unit from your opponent’s army destroys that unit, that enemy unit gains 3XP.\n\nAt the end of the battle, if that unit is not destroyed, this Thread of Fate ends successfully.\n\n**Identity Blurs (Waning):** At the start of the first battle round, select two AELDARI INFANTRY units from your Crusade army (excluding CHARACTERS) that are on the battlefield or embarked within TRANSPORTS that are on the battlefield. These must be GUARDIANS units if possible. Each time a unit from your opponent’s army destroys one of those units, that enemy unit gains 1XP. At the end of the battle, if both of those units are not destroyed, this Thread of Fate ends successfully. If only one of those units is not destroyed, roll one D6: on a 4+, this Thread of Fate ends successfully.\n\n**Fallen Hero (Frayed):** At the start of the first battle round, select one AELDARI PSYKER model from your Crusade army.\n\nIn your Command phase, if that PSYKER model is within 6\" of the centre of the battlefield, roll one D6: on a 4+, that PSYKER model is able to find the spirit stone and this Thread of Fate ends successfully."
      },
      "Ability§Thread of Fate: Enemy of My Enemy": {
        "text": "**Unknowing Ally (Dawning):** At the start of the first battle round, your opponent must select three units from their army that are on the battlefield or embarked within a TRANSPORT that is on the battlefield. Randomly determine one of those units to be the unknowing ally.\n\nAt the end of the battle, if that unit has not been destroyed, this Thread of Fate ends successfully.\n\n**Subtle Persuasions (Waning):** At the start of the first battle round, select three enemy units (excluding TRANSPORTS). In your Command phase, for each of those enemy units that have not been influenced, you can select one AELDARI PSYKER model from your Crusade army that is within 9\" of that enemy unit. That PSYKER model takes a Leadership test: if passed, that enemy unit becomes influenced. At the end of the battle, if all of those enemy units have been influenced, this Thread of Fate ends successfully.\n\n**Gift of Life (Frayed):** At the start of the Deploy Crusade Armies step, select one unit from your Crusade army and one objective marker within your deployment zone. In your Command phase, if that unit is not destroyed and is not within range of that objective marker, remove that objective marker from the battlefield.\n\nAt the end of the battle, if that objective marker is on the battlefield, this Thread of Fate ends successfully."
      },
      "Ability§Thread of Fate: Cleanse the Corruption": {
        "text": "**Whispers of Warning (Dawning):** At the start of the Deploy Crusade Armies step, select one AELDARI unit from your Crusade army (this must be an INFANTRY unit if possible) to be your Crusade army’s messenger. Set that unit up anywhere on the battlefield wholly within 6\" of the centre of the battlefield. If a unit from your opponent’s army destroys that unit, that enemy unit gains 3XP.\n\nAt the end of the battle, if that unit is wholly within your deployment zone, this Thread of Fate ends successfully.\n\n**Follow the Trail (Waning):** At the start of the Deploy Crusade Armies step, select two objective markers on the battlefield wholly within No Man’s Land. Each of the selected objective markers starts without the signs read. In your Command phase, for each of the selected objective markers without the signs read that you control, roll one D6: on a 5+, the signs are read at that objective marker.\n\nAt the end of the battle, if both selected objective markers had the signs read at them, this Thread of Fate ends successfully.\n\n**Into Peril (Frayed):** At the end of the battle, if three or more AELDARI units from your Crusade army (excluding Battle-shocked and TRANSPORT units) are wholly within your opponent’s deployment zone and at least one of those units is a CHARACTER unit, this Thread of Fate ends successfully."
      },
      "Ability§Thread of Fate: Isha’s Bounty": {
        "text": "**Author of Destruction (Dawning):** At the start of the first battle round, your opponent must select one unit from their army that is on the battlefield or is embarked within a TRANSPORT that is on the battlefield. This must be a MONSTER or VEHICLE unit if possible (excluding Dedicated Transports).\n\nAt the end of the third battle round, if that enemy unit is destroyed, this Thread of Fate ends successfully.\n\n**World Spirit (Waning):** At the start of the Deploy Crusade Armies step, select six objective markers on the battlefield to be world spirit nodes.\n\nAt the end of the battle, if you control at least half of the world spirit nodes objective markers, this Thread of Fate ends successfully.\n\n**Precious Remnants (Frayed):** At the end of the battle, if there are one or more AELDARI CHARACTER models from your Crusade army (excluding Battle-shocked models) wholly within each of the following areas of the battlefield, this Thread of Fate ends successfully: your deployment zone; No Man’s Land; your opponent’s deployment zone.\n\n### Results Stage\n\nWhen you reach this stage, your Crusade force will gain rewards based on how successful it was in avoiding impending disaster. First, consult the table below, using your Crusade forces final Threat to determine the reward you gain. Your Crusade force is then no longer Guiding Fate, until you choose to do so again.\n\nTHREAT\n\n0-4"
      },
      "Thread of Fate§Thread of Fate 1": {
        "text": "Roll a D6 for each Thread when you begin Guiding Fate (re-roll duplicates): 1 Destined Device, 2 Rising Nemesis, 3 Humble Beginnings, 4 Enemy of My Enemy, 5 Cleanse the Corruption, 6 Isha’s Bounty. Each Thread runs Dawning → Waning → Frayed; ending it in a battle (Fulcrum of Fate Agenda) reduces Threat by 3 / 2 / 1 by stage.",
        "rules": {
          "thread0": {
            "actions": [
              {
                "actionType": "add",
                "iterations": 1,
                "paths": [
                  [
                    "{self}",
                    "traits"
                  ]
                ],
                "value": "Ability§Thread of Fate: Destined Device"
              }
            ],
