      "Guiding Fate§Guiding Fate": {
        "assets": {
          "traits": [
            "Thread of Fate§Thread of Fate 1",
            "Thread of Fate§Thread of Fate 2",
            "Thread of Fate§Thread of Fate 3"
          ]
        },
        "text": "**Guiding Fate.** If your Crusade force includes ASURYANI or HARLEQUINS models and is not Guiding Fate, it can begin: set Threat to 1 and generate three Threads of Fate. At the end of each battle add D3 to Threat (3 if you lost). With the Fulcrum of Fate Agenda you can attempt to end one Thread; success reduces Threat by 3 (Dawning), 2 (Waning) or 1 (Frayed). If Threat reaches 13 every Thread ends in failure. When all three Threads have ended, apply the results below (if all three failed, Threat becomes at least 13) and your force is no longer Guiding Fate.\n\n**Threat 0-4 — Brief Respite:** Your Crusade force gains D3+2RP. You can select one ASURYANI PSYKER unit from your Crusade force to gain the PATH OF THE SEER keyword if it does not have it already. You can select one AUTARCH or AUTARCH WAYLEAPER unit from your Crusade force to gain the PATH OF COMMAND keyword if it does not have it already. You can select up to three ASURYANI INFANTRY units from your Crusade force to gain the PATH OF THE WARRIOR keyword if they do not have it already. You can select up to six ASURYANI units from your Crusade force to each gain one of the Aeldari Paths Battle Traits.\n\n**Threat 5-8 — Watchful:** Your Crusade force gains D3RP. You can select one ASURYANI PSYKER unit from your Crusade force to gain the PATH OF THE SEER keyword if it does not have it already, or you can select one AUTARCH or AUTARCH WAYLEAPER unit from your Crusade force to gain the PATH OF COMMAND keyword if it does not have it already. You can select up to two ASURYANI INFANTRY units from your Crusade force to gain the PATH OF THE WARRIOR keyword if they do not have it already. You can select up to four ASURYANI units from your Crusade force to each gain one of the Aeldari Paths Battle Traits.\n\n**Threat 9-12 — Beset:** Your Crusade force gains 1RP. You can select one AUTARCH or AUTARCH WAYLEAPER unit from your Crusade force to gain the PATH OF COMMAND keyword if it does not have it already. You can select one ASURYANI INFANTRY unit from your Crusade force to gain the PATH OF THE WARRIOR keyword if it does not have it already. You can select up to two ASURYANI units from your Crusade force to each gain one of the Aeldari Paths Battle Traits.\n\n**Threat 13+ — Endure The Inevitable:** Select one unit from your Crusade force to gain 2 Battle Scars and two other units from your Crusade force to gain 1 Battle Scar each."
      }
    },
    "gameModes": {},
    "theme": {}
  }
